-  "description": "# Cost-Aware Benchmark Price Dataset\n\nThis dataset links model benchmark performance, historical inference prices, and benchmark token usage to estimate the cost of running frontier language model benchmarks over time.\n\n## Contents\n\nThe dataset contains 342 model-price observations covering model metadata, benchmark scores, historical Artificial Analysis prices, Epoch AI benchmark token usage, and derived benchmark-cost estimates.\n\n## Main fields\n\n- `Model`: model name\n- `Model Slug`: normalized model identifier\n- `Creator`: model creator or provider\n- `License`: open/proprietary status\n- `GPQA Diamond (Scientific Reasoning)`: benchmark score\n- `AIME 2024 (Competition Math)`: benchmark score\n- `input_tokens_epoch_gpqa`, `output_tokens_epoch_gpqa`: Epoch AI token usage for GPQA-Diamond\n- `input tokens swe`, `output tokens swe`: Epoch AI token usage for SWE-bench Verified\n- `oneshot_AIME`, `epoch_gpqa`, `epoch_swe`: Epoch AI's measured benchmark scores\n- monthly price columns: historical input/output prices from Artificial Analysis snapshots\n- derived cost columns: estimated benchmark-level inference costs computed from token usage and historical prices\n\n## Sources\n\nBenchmark scores and token-usage data are derived from the Epoch AI Benchmarking Hub. Historical input and output token prices are collected from Artificial Analysis snapshots via the Internet Archive. Cache-token prices, where used, are collected from model-provider pricing pages.\n\n## Intended use\n\nThe dataset is intended for cost-aware analysis of language model evaluation, including estimating price-performance trends over time, benchmark cost at fixed performance, frontier benchmark costs, progress under fixed inference budgets, and diffusion of benchmark capabilities across the model ecosystem.\n\n## License and upstream terms\n\nThis dataset combines author-created derived fields with upstream benchmark and pricing data. Author-created metadata, cleaning decisions, derived variables, and documentation are released under CC BY 4.0. Analysis code is released separately under the MIT license. Epoch AI Benchmarking Hub data is used under CC BY 4.0 with attribution to Epoch AI. Artificial Analysis price data is attributed to Artificial Analysis. The authors do not claim ownership of Artificial Analysis source fields or relicense them. Artificial Analysis-derived fields remain subject to Artificial Analysis's applicable terms and policies. Users should attribute both this dataset and the relevant upstream sources when using the data.\n\n## Limitations\n\nThe dataset does not measure provider marginal costs, private negotiated prices, training costs, latency-adjusted costs, or causal effects of architecture or licensing. Some historical prices are missing because archived pages were unavailable or incomplete. Cache-token prices are only partially observed historically. Some benchmark/model combinations have limited coverage, especially for open-weight models on SWE-bench Verified.\n\n## Reproducibility\n\nThe accompanying code repository contains scripts to reproduce the paper's main tables and figures from this dataset. The dataset analysis can be run in several minutes on a personal computer.\n\n## Citation\n\nIf you use this dataset, please cite the accompanying paper and attribute the upstream data sources: Epoch AI Benchmarking Hub and Artificial Analysis.\n",
